      "message": "They exist to be sure that the constructor *did* make them empty, and to document to a reader that in this if/else tree, the *if* case doesn\u0027t need to set the spans, but the else case does. The idea is that now the if/else reads as a parallel construction -- we ensure in each case that the spans are in a known state.",
