      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand this. Adding 1 to this puts the data ... where? This mentions allocated data, but I\u0027m not seeing that allocation.\n\nedit: I see SkPathData::Alloc does the new. Is the +1 right? AFAIK, the SkRefCnt part adds 4 bytes for the fRefCnt field. Are we properly aligned by adding 1? I also have some vague questions about if this should be `std::launder` (or a related function), similar to how we do `SkAnySubclass`",
